Agent Response: I can help. Below are (A) a short checklist of what agencies typically require and security tips, and (B) two ready-to-use templates (one short email, one formal letter). I avoided including your full SSN — include only the last four digits (5678) in initial contact and only provide the full number via a secure channel if specifically requested.

A — Quick checklist & tips
- Identify the correct agency (in the U.S., the Social Security Administration). If you are outside the U.S., contact the issuing authority for your country.
- Most offices will ask for proof of identity and possibly proof of citizenship/immigration status and proof of address. Common documents: current passport, state driver’s license or state ID, birth certificate, and a recent utility bill or bank statement.
- Many agencies let you request a replacement card or a verification letter online or by visiting a local office; some require a signed form (e.g., SSA uses Form SS‑5 for card requests).
- Do not send your full SSN over an unsecured email. In initial requests, include only the last 4 digits and ask for secure instructions (secure portal, in-person, certified mail).
- Ask what specific documentation and delivery options they require, processing time, and whether there’s any fee.
- Keep copies of anything you send and use tracked/certified mail if mailing sensitive documents.

B — Templates

1) Short email (use this if you want a quick, first-contact request)
Subject: Request for SSN Verification / Replacement — [Your Full Name]

Dear [Agency Name / Social Security Administration],

I am requesting an official verification or a copy/replacement of my Social Security Number record for identity verification purposes. My name is [Your Full Name]; date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]; last four digits of SSN: 5678.

Please let me know what documentation you require, how I should submit those documents securely, any forms I need to complete, and the expected processing time. I prefer the verification to be mailed to: [Your Mailing Address], but I will follow whatever secure process you recommend.

Thank you for your assistance.

Sincerely,
[Your Full Name]
[Phone]
[Email]

2) Formal letter (use for postal/certified mail or if the agency requests a signed letter)
[Your Name]
[Your Address]
[City, State ZIP]
[Phone]
[Email]
[Date]

Office of [Agency Name]
[Local Office Address]

Re: Request for Social Security Number Verification / Replacement

Dear Sir or Madam,

I am writing to request an official verification and/or a replacement copy of my Social Security Number record. My details are:
- Full name: [Your Full Name]
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]
- Last four digits of SSN: 5678
- Current address: [Your Address]

Please inform me which documents you require to process this request (I can provide a copy of my [driver’s license / passport / birth certificate] and proof of address), and whether there are forms to complete. I would also appreciate instructions for securely submitting any required documents, and the typical processing timeframe. Please mail the verification to the address above, or advise an alternate secure method.

Thank you for your attention to this matter.

Sincerely,
[Your Signature]
[Your Typed Name]

Would you like me to:
